<%- include('../partials/header', { title, navActive: '' }) %>

<main class="product-page">
  <div style="max-width:760px;margin:0 auto">
    <div style="background:var(--amber-soft);border-left:4px solid var(--amber);padding:16px 20px;border-radius:8px;margin-bottom:28px">
      <strong style="color:var(--amber)">⚠ Educational Demo</strong>
      <p style="margin:4px 0 0;color:var(--text)">
        This section demonstrates SQL injection for CS 4347 Assignment 5.
        The vulnerable route is intentionally insecure. The safe route shows the fix.
        Both run as a read-only MySQL account — no data can be modified.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h1 style="font-size:40px;margin-bottom:8px">SQL Injection Demo</h1>
    <p style="color:var(--muted);margin-bottom:32px">
      An <strong>Order Lookup</strong> form searches orders by email and phone number.
      The vulnerable version concatenates user input directly into SQL;
      the safe version uses prepared statements with <code>?</code> placeholders.
    </p>

    <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:20px;margin-bottom:36px">
      <a href="/sqli/vulnerable" class="panel" style="display:block;text-decoration:none;background:var(--surface);border-radius:var(--radius);padding:24px;border:2px solid var(--amber)">
        <h2 style="color:var(--amber);font-size:22px;margin-bottom:8px">Vulnerable Route</h2>
        <p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:14px">
          Builds SQL by string concatenation. Shows the exact query executed. Injection works here.
        </p>
        <span class="btn" style="background:var(--amber);margin-top:12px">Try it →</span>
      </a>
      <a href="/sqli/safe" class="panel" style="display:block;text-decoration:none;background:var(--surface);border-radius:var(--radius);padding:24px;border:2px solid var(--green)">
        <h2 style="color:var(--green);font-size:22px;margin-bottom:8px">Safe Route</h2>
        <p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:14px">
          Uses <code>pool.execute()</code> with <code>?</code> placeholders. Shows template SQL and bound values. Injection fails here.
        </p>
        <span class="btn" style="margin-top:12px">Try it →</span>
      </a>
    </div>

    <div style="background:var(--surface);border-radius:var(--radius);padding:24px">
      <h2 style="font-size:22px;margin-bottom:16px">Demo Payloads</h2>
      <p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:14px;margin-bottom:16px">
        Try these on the <strong>Vulnerable</strong> route. Then try them on the <strong>Safe</strong> route and observe the difference.
      </p>

      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>#</th><th>Email field</th><th>Phone field</th><th>Effect</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>1</td>
            <td><code>olivia.martinez@example.com' #</code></td>
            <td><em>(anything wrong)</em></td>
            <td>Returns Olivia's 7 orders without knowing her phone. The <code>#</code> comments out the <code>AND u.phone_no = …</code> condition entirely.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>2</td>
            <td><code>x' OR 1=1 #</code></td>
            <td><em>(anything)</em></td>
            <td>Returns <strong>every</strong> order in the database — the <code>OR 1=1</code> always evaluates true.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>3</td>
            <td>olivia.martinez@example.com</td>
            <td>(214) 917-2915</td>
            <td>Legitimate query — returns Olivia's orders only when both fields are correct (same 7 rows as payload 1, but for the right reason).</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </div>
</main>

</body>
</html>
